\ 4x\\text{ }-\\text{ }5y &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFor a $2\\times 2$ system like the one above, we put the coefficients of the system into a $2\\times 2$ matrix, called the **coefficient matrix**:\n\n$$\nA = \\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{red}{2}} & {\\color{red}{3}} \\\\ {\\color{red}{4}} & {\\color{red}{-5}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nEach row has the coefficients of one of the equations in the system, and each column consists of the coefficients of one particular variable.\nWe also have the $2\\times 1$ column vectors\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{blue}{5}} \\\\ {\\color{blue}{-1}}\\end{bmatrix} \\quad \\text{and} \\quad\n\\mathbf{x}=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{b}$ consists of each constant on the right side of the system and $\\mathbf{x}$ contains the variables.\nWith these matrices, we can write our system as $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ or\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{red}{2}} & {\\color{red}{3}} \\\\ {\\color{red}{4}} & {\\color{red}{-5}}\\end{bmatrix}\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\n=\\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{blue}{5}} \\\\ {\\color{blue}{-1}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWe can write any system of two equations with two variables in this form.\nJust to check that the above equation is true, let's multiply out the left-hand side to see if it equals the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2x+3y \\\\ 4x\\text{ }-\\text{ }5y\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =b\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139541356 17592186576411 true] [17592186116490 1064 "Matrices can be used to represent systems of equations, such as the following:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+3y &=5 \\\\ 4x\\text{ }-\\text{ }5y &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFor a $2\\times 2$ system like the one above, we put the coefficients of the system into a $2\\times 2$ matrix, called the **coefficient